00:11:43,665 --> 00:11:46,095
You can use a check
config script

266
00:11:46,095 --> 00:11:48,825
that will find all the
necessary kernel packages,

267
00:11:48,825 --> 00:11:51,240
including the ones we
just discussed for

268
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,940
cgroup and overlay and add
that to your kernel build.

269
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,875
Then you build with a new kernel

270
00:11:55,875 --> 00:11:58,050
and you can run and
