279
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:26,010
When would you want to use

280
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:27,795
containers in
embedded development?

281
00:12:27,795 --> 00:12:29,430
There are really two
different places

282
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:31,545
where they are very useful.

283
00:12:31,545 --> 00:12:34,305
One is when you're
developing on a host system.

284
00:12:34,305 --> 00:12:35,820
So if you want to
create a consistent

285
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,215
Build and development
environment,

286
00:12:37,215 --> 00:12:38,880
you have multiple
developers who might be

287
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,740
building an
application and let's

288
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:43,230
say that application has a
bunch of dependencies and

289
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:44,520
specific libraries that need to

290
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,515
be installed in
order to build it.

291
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:48,210
You can either give people

292
00:12:48,210 --> 00:12:49,950
instructions or
scripts that tried to

293
00:12:49,950 --> 00:12:53,400
install those versions on
their operating system.

294
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,470
Or you can just
set up a container

295
00:12:55,470 --> 00:12:57,360
that builds with the exact
versions that you care

296
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,220
about and everyone
can share the copy of

297
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,570
the container and build with

298
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:02,310
exactly the same Build system.

299
00:13:02,310 --> 00:13:04,110
It's also really
useful for creating

300
00:13:04,110 --> 00:13:05,730
automated test
frameworks because you

301
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:09,810
can know that any
new automated tests

302
00:13:09,810 --> 00:13:11,190
that you run is always using

303
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:14,384
the same environment and you
can easily add new systems

304
00:13:14,384 --> 00:13:16,950
that will again be using the
exact same components you

305
00:13:16,950 --> 00:13:20,445
use when you build on
your development system.

306
00:13:20,445 --> 00:13:22,770
Then you can deploy

307
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:23,790
what test frameworks to

308
00:13:23,790 --> 00:13:25,710
continuous integration
and deployment,

309
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:28,050
and there's more
information about that in

310
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:30,810
the continuous integration
deployments section

311
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:33,970
of the test videos.

312
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,575
Then in terms of on
the target system.

313
00:13:37,575 --> 00:13:39,360
On our target system
that's actually

314
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,565
running our embedded Linux OS,

315
00:13:41,565 --> 00:13:43,785
when would you want to
use a container there?

316
00:13:43,785 --> 00:13:46,230
This can be useful for

317
00:13:46,230 --> 00:13:48,885
pulling independencies
quickly for test purposes.

318
00:13:48,885 --> 00:13:50,340
Let's say you're testing out

319
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:53,385
some application that
is supported on Ubuntu,

320
00:13:53,385 --> 00:13:55,920
but isn't, maybe has

321
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:58,905
some components that aren't
supported by Buildroot today.

322
00:13:58,905 --> 00:14:00,600
Before you go
through the process

323
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,620
of actually implementing

324
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:04,110
all those recipes and
adding to Buildroot,

325
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:07,005
you could just using Docker,

326
00:14:07,005 --> 00:14:10,635
bring up on Ubuntu
instance on Buildroot.

327
00:14:10,635 --> 00:14:12,300
Then once you have the Ubuntu

328
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,440
instance running on Buildroot,

329
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,540
you could use sudo
apt-get install to

330
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:19,260
install the dependencies and
test locally on the device.

331
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:22,440
You can also use
it for supporting

332
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,755
optional or possibly conflicting
product configuration.

333
00:14:25,755 --> 00:14:27,960
Maybe there's a
specific version of

334
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,520
a Python library
that you need for

335
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,680
some application that you're
going to run on the target.

336
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,780
You could use Docker to bring

337
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:35,820
in that exact environment
that might be

338
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,890
different from the
environment that you have

339
00:14:37,890 --> 00:14:41,010
for your own applications
running on target.

340
00:14:41,010 --> 00:14:43,020
You could also maybe bring in

341
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:46,005
multiple web servers
or applications.

342
00:14:46,005 --> 00:14:49,440
Maybe you'd have one
main web server that

343
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:53,220
serves up content from
your device on port 80,

344
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:55,770
but you can bring in a
second one that served up

345
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:57,120
some other content based on

346
00:14:57,120 --> 00:15:00,520
a pre-built container
on some other port.